ve the potential to deliver biomolecular single-particle imaging, similar to cryo-electron microscopy but without the need for cryo-fixation and with temporal resolution from femtoseconds to milliseconds. While this possibility was recognized b</description><guid isPermaLink="false">cab8f0811f2b</guid><pubDate>2026-10-09T11:16:19.424988+00:00</pubDate><source>arXiv 光学与光子学 (physics.optics)</source><category>激光</category></item></channel></rss>